# Build output
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# All user-supplied game data lives here and is NEVER committed.
# `/data/*` rather than `/data/`: git cannot re-include a file from inside an
# excluded directory, so the directory itself must stay traversable.
/data/*
!/data/README.md
!/data/**/README.md

# Trace captures a ground-truth test names, per ADR-0046. The directory has to
# be re-included first and its contents re-excluded, for the same reason line 8
# uses `/data/*`: git will not descend into an excluded directory, so a `!` on a
# file inside one never fires. Then each capture is named individually - never a
# glob: a new capture stays untracked until someone adds its name here, in the
# same change that adds the test naming it. Every other capture (the exploratory
# hd-trail-* sets, and anything taken to answer a question rather than to pin a
# test) stays excluded by the `/data/traces/*` line below.
!/data/traces/
/data/traces/*
!/data/traces/pad0-boost.csv
!/data/traces/talons-junction-steer-lean.csv
!/data/traces/talons-junction-pitch-both-ways.csv
!/data/traces/talons-junction-standing-start.csv
!/data/traces/talons-junction-time-trial-lap.csv
!/data/traces/talons-junction-time-trial-lap-omega.csv
!/data/traces/talons-junction-clean-lap.csv
!/data/traces/venom-straight.csv

# Belt-and-braces: even outside /data/, no game content may ever be committed.
# These patterns exist so a stray copy in the wrong directory still gets caught.
*.chd
*.iso
*.cso
*.pkg
*.pbp
*.umd
*.wad
*.elf
*.prx
*.self
*.BIN
*.bin
*.img
*.gcm
*.vpk
*.edat

# PS3 and Vita. HD/Fury and 2048 ship PSARC archives rather than WADs, their
# modules are `.sprx`/`.suprx`/`.skprx`, and `.dkey` is the PS3 disc key - not
# content itself, but the one thing that decrypts a disc image.
*.psarc
*.sprx
*.suprx
*.skprx
*.dkey
*.key

# SMAA's own precomputed lookup textures (AreaTex/SearchTex), MIT-licensed
# third-party shader data - not extracted disc content. See
# scripts/check-leakage.py's ALLOWED_TRACKED, which must stay in sync.
!/crates/render/src/post/smaa_area.bin
!/crates/render/src/post/smaa_search.bin

# Reproductions this project itself writes, not just source content: a
# `--screenshot` is a rendering of the disc's models and textures, and the
# movie cache demuxes to these four formats (crates/game/src/movie.rs). See
# scripts/check-leakage.py, which is the single source of truth this list
# must stay in sync with.
*.png
*.ivf
!/crates/formats/tests/data/testsrc-64x64.ivf
*.h264
*.ipu
*.pss
*.mip
*.vex
*.fnt
*.pmf

# Packaged builds and the packaging tool. `just appimage` writes into
# data/appimage/, which /data/* already covers; this catches an AppImage built
# with --out somewhere else, since no binary is ever committed either.
*.AppImage

# Ghidra. Note: deliberately NOT `*.lock`, which would swallow Cargo.lock.
# This workspace commits Cargo.lock. A project opened in the repository root
# leaves its lock beside the `.gpr`, not inside `*.rep/`, and that lock records
# the developer's hostname and username, hence the explicit pattern.
*.gpr
*.rep/
/OpenAntiGrav.lock*

# Emulator state
*.ppst
*.p2s
*.sav
*.state
*.state[0-9]

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Python bytecode from scripts/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Agents
.claude/

# A Ghidra project holds the executable's own bytes, so it is game content by
# ADR-0006 and must never be tracked. `data/ghidra/` was already covered by the
# blanket `/data/` rule; this covers a project copied in from another machine.
/vimes-ghidra/
*.rep/
*.gpr
*.lock
scratch-*.md

# Session scratch space (agent-local tmpfiles, not build output).
/tmp/
